{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Returns Go function symbols recovered from the pclntab embedded in a (possibly stripped) ELF, PE or thin Mach-O: is_go, the header magic (go_version_magic), a pclntab block (file_offset, version 1.2/1.16/1.18/1.20, pointer_size, header-declared function_count), a bounded functions[] list (name, entry virtual address, mapped file_offset or null) with function_coverage, and heuristic package_names with package_coverage. It reads the file once without executing the target, without network access, and without writing files; a universal Mach-O requires selecting a thin slice. It does NOT disassemble, recover types/moduledata/typelinks/inlined frames, read non-pclntab symbol tables, or establish reachability or current validity; names are observed table bytes and packages are inferred name prefixes. Resource guards: 256 MiB input cap, max_functions (default 20000, max 200000) with the remainder reported through function_coverage, a 16 MiB structural-table budget, and an 8 MiB inline-output cap. Unknowns are explicit: no decodable table -> is_go false with empty lists and null magic/pclntab; a non-file-backed entry -> file_offset null; absence of a pclntab is not proof the file is not Go.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"path":"/artifacts/application"},{"max_functions":5000,"path":"/artifacts/application","slice":"arm64"}],"properties":{"max_functions":{"default":20000,"description":"Maximum recovered functions to return inline; the remainder is reported through function_coverage","maximum":200000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"Absolute filesystem path to the selected local file","minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"},"slice":{"description":"Architecture of the Mach-O universal slice to analyze; defaults to the first declared slice","e